  "_comment": "Default file-icon theme. Values are icon names resolving to assets/{ns}/ui/icons/{name}.svg. A resource pack overrides this by shipping the same path.",
  "_icons": "IntelliJ Platform icons (Apache 2.0, JetBrains s.r.o.) -- see ui/icons/ATTRIBUTION.md. They carry their own palette, so filetypes.css does NOT tint them; it colours the row label and anything monochrome. A theme that wants them flattened to one colour can say icon(\"...\", monochrome) in CSS.",
  "_gap": "Kotlin, Python, TypeScript, Rust, Go, C/C++, Ruby, PHP, shell, SQL, Markdown and GLSL have no icon in the IntelliJ PLATFORM set -- theirs live in per-language plugin modules. They are still listed below, resolving to the plain text document, because listing them is what gives each its own .filetype-* class for the cascade.",

